#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""yt-ascii: stream video through a portable terminal visual renderer.

Usage:
    yt-ascii [url] [options]      # omit the url for an interactive paste prompt

Keys (while playing):
    space        pause / resume
    p            cycle character palette
    s            cycle visual style
    e            cycle compatible visual effect
    ← / →        seek -5s / +5s
    ↓ / ↑        seek -30s / +30s
    0..9         jump to 0%..90% of the video
    q / Ctrl-C   quit

Needs NumPy and yt-dlp. The supported installer supplies those plus an FFmpeg
fallback through imageio-ffmpeg in a private environment; audio additionally
wants ffplay on PATH. Runs on Linux, macOS and Windows.
"""
